<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sylvain Roux</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1823">1823</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sylvain Roux (died 1823) was a French colonial agent who led the reoccupation of Île Sainte-Marie, off the north-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, from 1818 and became its first commandant. He set up a post at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambodifotatra">Ambodifotatra</a> as a base for trade and for French claims on the Malagasy coast, and died on the island.</p></div>
